  "extraction_notes": [
    "The PDF identifies the device as a -20 V P-channel enhancement MOSFET. Signed P-channel voltage and current values are stored as magnitudes, while source signs remain in the test conditions.",
    "Typical source_kind is used only for values in the PDF Typ column or for the labeled Typical Characteristic Curves. Minimum and maximum table values remain minimum or maximum.",
    "Curve points are approximate digitizations of visible target-specific traces on PDF page 3. No curve points were extrapolated beyond the plotted axes.",
    "Figure 2 explicitly identifies 25 C and 125 C transfer curves. Figures 1, 3, and 5 do not identify curve temperature, so the electrical table heading of TA=25 C was not applied to those unlabeled curves.",
    "The capacitance table values are typical at VGS=0 V, VDS=-10 V, and f=1 MHz. The capacitance curves do not state frequency on the figure, so that condition is not asserted for the digitized sweep."
  ],
